Eligibility for the Outreachy program is as follows:

The current round of internships is open internationally to women (cis and
trans), trans men, and genderqueer people. Additionally, it's open to
residents and nationals of the United States of any gender who are
Black/African American, Hispanic/Latin@, American Indian, Alaska Native,
Native Hawaiian, or Pacific Islander.

If you don't qualify for the internship program, you are welcome to work
through the tutorial and submit patches in the normal way, ie not via the
Outreachy mailing list, but to the maintainers, obtained using the
get_maintainer program.  If you have any questions about this, please feel
free to send me a direct email.

You may also be interested in the Eudyptula Challenge, which is a guided
and challenging pathway into Linux kernel development:

http://eudyptula-challenge.org/

